msgid "Images"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mbr-isa.php:1207
msgid "Index images from the Media Library."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mbr-isa.php:1210
msgid "Images are indexed on their alt text, caption, description and filename — everything a person has written about the picture. Nothing is read from the image itself. Results link to the page the image appears on, not to the file."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mbr-isa.php:1213
msgid "JPEG, PNG, GIF, WebP and AVIF. SVG files are not indexed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mbr-isa.php:1218
msgid "Which images"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mbr-isa.php:1223
msgid "Images published somewhere on the site (recommended)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mbr-isa.php:1225
msgid "Indexed when a published, unprotected page either owns the image or displays it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mbr-isa.php:1230
msgid "Only images attached to a published page or post (strict)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mbr-isa.php:1232
msgid "Uses the WordPress attachment relationship only. Images added through Media &rsaquo; Add New, or brought in by an import, are excluded even where pages display them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mbr-isa.php:1237
msgid "Every image in the Media Library"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mbr-isa.php:1239
msgid "Rarely what you want. A Media Library accumulates logos, backgrounds, superseded artwork and images uploaded to pages that were never published — all of which become searchable under this setting."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mbr-isa.php:1246
msgid "Image alt text"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mbr-isa.php:1250
msgid "Only index images that have alt text."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mbr-isa.php:1253
msgid "Alt text is the one field written specifically to describe what is in the picture, so it is by some distance the best thing to search on. Leaving this ticked indexes the images somebody has described and skips the rest."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-mbr-isa.php:1256
msgid "Untick it and a caption, a description, or a filename that actually says something will do instead. Filenames like IMG_4821 or screenshot-2026-08-18 are ignored either way — they would only ever match the wrong thing."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: eligible count, 2: number of images tested, 3: total images in the library
#: includes/class-mbr-isa.php:1265
msgid "%1$d of the %2$d most recent images tested (%3$d in the Media Library)."
msgstr ""

